course: dictionary
lesson: 187
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word air has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is meant. «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air.» Here air is the mix of gases we breathe, all around us but too small to see.
explain: «Throw it in the air» means the space above the ground. «To air a room» is a verb: it means to let fresh air in. «She had an air of calm» means the way someone seems.
explain: Ask yourself: what does the sentence show? If the sentence is about breathing or pollution, air is the gas. If it is about flying or throwing, air is the space above the ground. Then put your meaning back into the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Air is a mix of gases. Most of it is nitrogen and oxygen.
fact: We breathe air, and we cannot see it, but it is all around us.
fact: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.»
fact: «Breathed-out air contains less oxygen and more carbon dioxide than breathed-in air.»
fact: «To air» a room means to let fresh air in, and «by air» means by plane.
exercise: «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air.» What does air mean here? | To let fresh air into a room | The way someone seems | *The mix of gases all around us | A tune that you hum
exercise: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels; they can be full of bad air.» What is air in this sentence? | *The gases we breathe, which can be unsafe | A way of looking | A kind of music | The space above the ground
exercise: Nadia opens the window to air the room. What does air mean? | *To let fresh air in | To breathe very hard | To hang up washing | To sing a tune
test: «Breathed-out air contains less oxygen and more carbon dioxide than breathed-in air.» Which is true? | Breathed-in and breathed-out air are exactly the same | Breathed-out air has no gas at all | *Breathed-out air has more carbon dioxide | Breathed-out air has more oxygen
test: «She had an air of calm, even when the test was hard.» What does air mean? | To let fresh air in | Space above the ground | A mix of gases | *The way someone seems
exam: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators.» What does «in the air» mean here? | Up a tree | *While flying in an aircraft | Sitting still on the ground | Under the water
